# Hover Color & Area Label UX — Design Spec

**Date:** 2026-06-22  
**Feature area:** Floor plan viewer — hover states and area labels  
**Scope:** `useFloorPlanLabels`, `useFloorPlanLayer`, `layer-definitions.ts`, consuming components

---

## Problem

The current hover and label behaviour is uniform across all contexts. In the editor the blue fill highlight distracts from editing, labels are always visible instead of on-demand, and there is no level-of-detail simplification at low zoom. In the public-facing map and preview modes the hover colour is too vivid, labels always appear regardless of zoom level, and hovering areas without names still triggers a colour change.

---

## Solution Overview

Introduce a `mode: "editor" | "preview" | "map"` prop on both `useFloorPlanLabels` and `useFloorPlanLayer`. Each mode applies a distinct set of hover and label rules. A `hoveredAreaId: string | null` prop (derived from the existing `hoveredFeatureId` store value) is forwarded from consuming components.

---

## Architecture

```
Editor3DMapView  → useFloorPlanLayer(mode="editor")
                 → useFloorPlanLabels(mode="editor", hoveredAreaId)
                   (mousemove handler: no name-gate needed in editor mode)

PreviewOverlay   → useFloorPlanLayer(mode="preview")
                 → useFloorPlanLabels(mode="preview", buildingName)
                   (mousemove handler: name-gate before setHoveredFeatureId)

PublicMapViewer  → useFloorPlanLayer(mode="map")
                 → useFloorPlanLabels(mode="map", buildingName)
                   (mousemove handler: name-gate before setHoveredFeatureId)
```

No Zustand store shape changes. `hoveredFeatureId` already exists in the store and is read at the component level, then forwarded as `hoveredAreaId` (editor only) or left in the store for the highlight layer filter (map/preview).

`buildingName` is read from the existing location/building data already available in the parent component (or from the store if it exposes a location name field). The implementation plan will confirm the exact source once the public map viewer and preview overlay are inspected.

---

## Mode Behaviours

### Editor Mode (`mode="editor"`)

**Hover fill colour**
- Disabled entirely.
- `applyHighlight` in `useFloorPlanLayer` becomes a no-op when `mode === "editor"`.
- Highlight layers remain in the map (no add/remove churn) but always match nothing.

**Area labels**
- Hidden by default — no labels drawn in the idle state.
- On hover: only the label for `hoveredAreaId` is drawn, at the same canvas position and style as existing labels (centroid, white text, dark halo).
- Labels disappear immediately when the cursor leaves the area.
- No animation.

**2D canvas editor tab**
- Out of scope. `NewFloorplanEditor` is a separate renderer and does not go through these hooks.

---

### Map & Preview Modes (`mode="preview"` | `mode="map"`)

**Hover fill colour — subtle**

New constants in `layer-definitions.ts`:
```ts
const HOVER_FILL_COLOR_SUBTLE   = "#e8f0fe"  // very light blue-grey
const HOVER_FILL_OPACITY_SUBTLE = 0.18
```

These replace the existing `#3b82f6` / `0.55` values on the 3D extrusion highlight layer in map and preview modes only. Flat (2D) mode highlight layers are unchanged.

**Name-gated hover fill**
- The event handler in each consuming component reads `e.features[0].properties.name` before calling `setHoveredFeatureId`.
- If the name is empty or absent, `setHoveredFeatureId(null)` is called — no fill appears.
- `applyHighlight` itself is unchanged; the gate is upstream at the event handler level.

**Zoom-adaptive labels**

Threshold constant (top of `useFloorPlanLabels.ts`):
```ts
const LABEL_DETAIL_ZOOM = 17.5
```

Zoom tracking: a `useEffect` registers a `zoom` map event listener, reads `map.getZoom()`, and stores the value in local React state (`currentZoom`). Runs only when `mode !== "editor"`.

| Zoom | Rendered labels |
|---|---|
| `< LABEL_DETAIL_ZOOM` | No area labels. Building/location name drawn at marker pin position (slightly larger text for legibility at low zoom). |
| `≥ LABEL_DETAIL_ZOOM` | All area labels rendered as today. |

The building name is passed via a new `buildingName: string` prop on `useFloorPlanLabels`.

**No zoom logic in editor mode** — zoom tracking is skipped entirely.

---

## Files Changed

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/lib/map/useFloorPlanLabels.ts` | Add `mode`, `hoveredAreaId`, `buildingName` props; branch draw loop by mode; add zoom listener |
| `src/lib/map/useFloorPlanLayer.ts` | Add `mode` prop; no-op `applyHighlight` in editor mode |
| `src/lib/map/layer-definitions.ts` | Add `HOVER_FILL_COLOR_SUBTLE`, `HOVER_FILL_OPACITY_SUBTLE` constants |
| `src/components/editor/Editor3DMapView.tsx` | Pass `mode="editor"`, `hoveredAreaId`; add name-gate in mousemove handler |
| `src/components/editor/PreviewOverlay.tsx` | Pass `mode="preview"`, `buildingName`; add name-gate in mousemove handler |
| Public map viewer component | Pass `mode="map"`, `buildingName`; add name-gate in mousemove handler |

---

## Out of Scope

- 2D canvas editor (`NewFloorplanEditor`) hover states
- Any animation on label appearance/disappearance
- Custom colour theming per area (hover colour is always the same subtle neutral)
- Mobile / touch hover states

---

## Constants Reference

```ts
// layer-definitions.ts
HOVER_FILL_COLOR_SUBTLE   = "#e8f0fe"
HOVER_FILL_OPACITY_SUBTLE = 0.18

// useFloorPlanLabels.ts
LABEL_DETAIL_ZOOM = 17.5
```

---

## Definition of Done

- [ ] Editor mode: hovering an area shows its label, no fill colour change
- [ ] Editor mode: no labels visible when not hovering
- [ ] Map/preview mode: hover fill is subtle (`#e8f0fe` at 0.18 opacity)
- [ ] Map/preview mode: hover fill does not appear on areas without a name
- [ ] Map/preview mode zoom < 17.5: only building name shown at marker position
- [ ] Map/preview mode zoom ≥ 17.5: all area labels shown as before
- [ ] No regression in existing label declutter / pin label behaviour
- [ ] Builds, lints, typechecks green
